# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Nothing here is required to run Notifyr:
# with no credentials it uses the in-memory store, which is the right thing for
# `npm run dev` and for the test suite.
#
# Setting BOTH of these switches the app to the shared Redis store
# (`createStore()` in src/lib/store.ts) — see docs/REDIS-STORE.md. Setting only
# one falls back to in-memory rather than building a client that fails on every
# request. Both values are in the "REST API" section of an Upstash database.

UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
